# FDEM Catalyst Center / DNAC Field Reference

This is the **single source of truth** for canonical field names of `cisco:dnac:*` and `cisco:catalyst:center:*` sourcetypes as confirmed against the FDEM (Florida Division of Emergency Management) production stack on 2026-05-08.

## Sourcetype onboarding status (FDEM, as of 2026-05-08; demo-stack reconfirm 2026-05-29)

The Catalyst Center TA exposes 11 sourcetypes total. FDEM has onboarded 9 of them; the two `:report` sourcetypes are pending on FDEM but **were confirmed present and populated on the demo `sh-i-ak` stack on 2026-05-29** — see field inventories below.

| Sourcetype | FDEM onboarded? | Demo stack onboarded? | Fields documented below? | Demo data available? |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `cisco:dnac:devicehealth` | ✅ Yes | ✅ Yes | ✅ Yes | ✅ Yes |
| `cisco:dnac:issue` | ✅ Yes | ✅ Yes | ✅ Yes | ✅ Yes |
| `cisco:dnac:client` | ✅ Yes | ✅ Yes | ✅ Yes | ✅ Yes |
| `cisco:dnac:clienthealth` | ✅ Yes | ✅ Yes | ✅ Yes | ✅ Yes |
| `cisco:dnac:networkhealth` | ✅ Yes | ✅ Yes | ✅ Yes | ✅ Yes |
| `cisco:dnac:compliance` | ✅ Yes | ✅ Yes | ✅ Yes | ✅ Yes |
| `cisco:dnac:audit:logs` | ✅ Yes | ✅ Yes | ✅ Yes | ✅ Yes |
| `cisco:dnac:securityadvisory` | ✅ Yes | ✅ Yes | ✅ Yes | ✅ Yes |
| `cisco:dnac:site:topology` | ✅ Yes (added 2026-05-08, passive/snapshot) | ✅ Yes | ✅ Yes | ✅ Yes |
| `cisco:catalyst:center:inventory:report` | ❌ Pending input add | ✅ Yes (4,460 events on sh-i-ak as of 2026-05-29) | ✅ Yes (see [Catalyst Center scheduled reports](#catalyst-center-scheduled-reports-cisco-catalyst-center-report)) | ✅ Yes |
| `cisco:catalyst:center:compliance:report` | ❌ Pending input add | ✅ Yes (4,440 events on sh-i-ak as of 2026-05-29) | ✅ Yes (see [Catalyst Center scheduled reports](#catalyst-center-scheduled-reports-cisco-catalyst-center-report)) | ✅ Yes |

**Implication for FDEM-tagged saved searches:** until the missing 2 are onboarded *at FDEM*, FDEM-targeted searches MUST use only the 9 confirmed sourcetypes above. Searches that depend on the `:report` sourcetypes will work against the demo stack today (and against any non-FDEM environment that has the inputs enabled) but must include a graceful fallback or be tagged as demo-only when shipped to FDEM.

## Catalyst Center scheduled reports (`cisco:catalyst:center:*:report`)

These sourcetypes carry the daily/scheduled reports emitted via Catalyst Center's **Reports** API (not the live monitoring endpoints that feed the other `cisco:dnac:*` sourcetypes). Each event is one row from the report. Field names follow the report's column headers — **spaces are preserved** for the inventory report, and the compliance report uses camelCase keys.

### `cisco:catalyst:center:inventory:report` (Daily Inventory Report)

Column-named fields (all contain spaces — single-quote in `eval()`):

| Field | Type | Example | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| `'Device Name'` | string | `corp-9300x-edge-05` | Stable per-device identifier; present on every event. |
| `'Device Type'` | string | `Cisco Catalyst 9300X-48HX Switch` | |
| `'Device Family'` | string | `Switches and Hubs` / `Unified AP` / `Routers` / `Wireless Controller` | Use for high-level inventory rollups. |
| `'Device Series'` | string | `Cisco Catalyst 9300X Series Switches` | Not present on every event; check `isnotnull` before using. |
| `'IP Address'` | string | `10.100.0.5` | |
| `'MAC Address'` | string | `02:0e:aa:cf:30:38` | Not present on every event. |
| `'Platform'` | string | `C9300X-48HX` | Not present on every event. |
| `'Software Type'` | string | `IOS-XE` | Not present on every event. |
| `'Software Version'` | string | `17.15.3` | Present on every event; suitable for version-distribution rollups. |
| `'Serial Number'` | string | `FCW0560DC54` | |
| `'Reachability Status'` | string | `Reachable` / `Unreachable` | Sparsely populated. |
| `'Manageability Status'` | string | `Managed` / `Unmanaged` | Sparsely populated. |
| `'Up Time'` | string | `277 days, 07:07:26.265` | Free-text duration string; parse with regex if needed. |
| `'Role'` | string | `BORDER ROUTER` / `ACCESS` / `DISTRIBUTION` | Sparsely populated. |
| `'Role Source'` | string | `AUTO` / `MANUAL` | |
| `'Site Hierarchy'` | string | `Global/USA/San-Jose-CA/East Wing/WAN-Edge` | Sparsely populated. Use with `dnac_site_normalize` if mixing FDEM and demo data. |
| `Hostname` | string | (matches `'Device Name'`) | Sparsely populated. |
| `'Image Version'` | string | `17.15.3` | Same value as `'Software Version'`. |
| `'Last Sync Time'` | epoch ms | `1780025620360` | Convert with `_time=strftime(...)`. |
| `'AP Floor'` | string | (for APs) | |
| `'Wlc Ip Address'` | string | (for APs) | Controller IP. |
| `cisco_catalyst_host` | string | `https://catalystcenter01.acme.example.com` | Source CC tenant. |
| `report_type` | string | `inventory` | |
| `report_name` | string | `Daily Inventory Report` | |
| `collection_timestamp` | epoch s | `1780027200` | |

**Coverage note:** field counts vary across events — the TA appears to emit some lighter records alongside full ones. About 55% of inventory events have `Hostname` / `Reachability Status` / `Site Hierarchy` populated; 100% have `Device Name` / `Device Family` / `IP Address` / `Software Version`. For rollups that depend on the richer fields, filter `where isnotnull('Hostname')` to keep only full records.

