| `` `index_security` `` | XDR, Cloud Security, ESA, WSA, Defender, SD-WAN UTD |
| `` `index_bms` `` | Building management |
| `` `index_dhcp` `` | DHCP server logs |
| `` `index_thousandeyes` `` | ThousandEyes |
| `` `index_f5` `` | F5 BIG-IP |

## Structural macros (Tier 3)

| Macro | Args | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `` `dnac_site_normalize(site)` `` | 1 (raw site path) | Normalize any DNAC site path to `"<Campus>: <Building>"` form. Already understands FDEM's TLH / AUB / SEOC / Betty Easley / Warehouse tokens. Returns empty string for null/blank/literal-"null". |
| `` `spaces_hierarchy(prefix)` `` | 1 (event prefix) | Walks Cisco Spaces firehose location tree (5 levels), exposes `floor`, `building`, `campus`, `site`. |

## Canonical site field per sourcetype

This is the table I keep getting wrong. **Memorize:**

| Sourcetype | Site field(s) | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `cisco:dnac:devicehealth` | `Site`, `Location` | `Site` is the canonical hierarchical path (e.g. `Global/Florida/Auburndale/AUB`). `Location` is alternate. Use `coalesce(Site, Location)`. |
| `cisco:dnac:issue` | `SiteName`, `SiteNameHierarchy`, `SiteType` | `SiteNameHierarchy` is the full path; `SiteName` is the short label. |
| `cisco:dnac:client` | `siteHierarchy`, `siteHierarchyId`, `siteId` | camelCase. `siteHierarchy` is the full path. |
| `cisco:dnac:clienthealth` | `siteId` ONLY | No path field. Lookup by ID required to label. |
| `cisco:dnac:networkhealth` | (none) | Global rollup, no per-site. |
| `cisco:dnac:compliance` | (none in field list) | Device-scoped only. |
| `cisco:dnac:audit:logs` | `network.siteId` | Dotted JSON path. |
| `cisco:dnac:securityadvisory` | (none) | Device-scoped only. |
| `cisco:dnac:site:topology` | `nameHierarchy`, `name`, `id`, `parentId` | `nameHierarchy` is the full path (e.g. `Global/Florida/Tallahassee/TLH`). `name` is the short label. `id`/`parentId` form the hierarchy graph. |

**Site normalization pattern (overwrite in place):**

```spl
# devicehealth
| eval Site=`dnac_site_normalize(coalesce(Site, Location))`

# issue
| eval SiteNameHierarchy=`dnac_site_normalize(SiteNameHierarchy)`

# client
| eval siteHierarchy=`dnac_site_normalize(siteHierarchy)`
```

